From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mckenna654 <mckenna654@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 18:03:46 +1100
Subject: Replace the battle menu words with picture buttons

The Little Trainer battle menu is now a row of large buttons drawn over the
message box: an attack star, a special-attack symbol that follows the move's
type (flame, drop, leaf, bolt, snowflake, rock, eye or sparkle), a Poke Ball
(or swap arrows against trainers) and a running shoe. A pulsing ring shows
the selection, a small star marks the recommended attack, the cursor starts
there on the first turn, and the move name is shown beside the row.

Also: attacks that cannot affect the opponent are never offered (a typeless
attack is borrowed instead), and the player's Pokemon take no recoil damage.

Art is original, generated by assets/ui/make_battle_icons.py.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>

